seconded by Chairman Montgomery, Member Theodore F. White as requested, was granted leave of absence for ninety days, beginning August 1st, 1886.

 On motion the following order was unanimously made:

 It is hereby ordered by the Supervisors of the county of Cochise, Territory of Arizona, on this the 18th day of July, A. D. 1886;

 That there be, and is hereby levied, a tax of 8 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county of Cochise, for territorial purposes;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of one dollar and seventy-two cents ($1.72) upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county for county purposes;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of .03 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the Territorial School Fund;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 45 cents, upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the County School Fund;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 30 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the Interest Redemption Fund;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 6 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the Building Interest Fund, to pay interest on bonds of said county issued for the purchase of land and the erection of court house and jail thereon;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of .05 cent on each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the Building Redemption Fund, for the redemption of the bonds of said county, issued for the purchase of land, and the erection of court house and jail thereon;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 15 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund known as the Interest Fund, to pay interest on certain Territorial bonds issued under act of the Territorial Legislature, approved March 5, 1883;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 6 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund, known as the Interest Fund, to pay interest on certain Territorial bonds issued under act of the Territorial Legislature, also approved March 5, 1883;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 4 cents upon each one hundred dollars assessed valuation of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund, known as the Redemption Sinking Fund, to create fund to pay the redemption bonds of said county;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 2 cents, upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund, known as the Normal School Fund, as required by an act of the last Territorial Legislature;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 10 cents, upon each one hundred dollars assessed valuation of taxable property, both real and personal, in said county, to be paid into the special fund, known as the Insane Asylum Fund, as required by an act of the last Territorial Legislature;

 And further, that there be, and is hereby levied an additional tax of 40 cents, upon each one hundred dollars assessed value of taxable property, both real and personal, in the School District embracing and including the city of Tombstone, in said county, to be paid into a special fund to pay interest on certain bonds issued by said county, for the support and maintenance of the public schools of said district, and for the redemption of certain of said bonds.

